# API Design Conventions

## Route Structure

```
POST   /auth/register
POST   /auth/login
POST   /auth/refresh
POST   /auth/logout

GET    /users/:id
PATCH  /users/me

POST   /guilds
GET    /guilds/:id
DELETE /guilds/:id
POST   /guilds/:id/invite
POST   /invites/:code/join
GET    /guilds/:id/members
DELETE /guilds/:id/members/:userId

POST   /guilds/:id/channels
PATCH  /channels/:id
DELETE /channels/:id

POST   /channels/:id/messages
GET    /channels/:id/messages?before=<cursor>&limit=50
PATCH  /messages/:id
DELETE /messages/:id

POST   /channels/:id/voice/token
```

## Response Format

All endpoints return the standard envelope:

```json
// Success
{ "data": { ... } }

// Error
{ "error": "human-readable message" }
```

## Status Codes

| Code | When |
|------|------|
| 200  | Successful GET, PATCH, DELETE |
| 201  | Successful POST that creates a resource |
| 204  | Successful operation with no response body |
| 400  | Validation error or malformed request |
| 401  | Missing or invalid authentication |
| 403  | Authenticated but not authorized |
| 404  | Resource not found |
| 409  | Conflict (duplicate username, already a member) |
| 429  | Rate limited |
| 500  | Unexpected server error |

## Pagination

Cursor-based for all list endpoints:

```
GET /channels/:id/messages?before=<messageId>&limit=50
```

Response includes whether more results exist:

```json
{ "data": { "items": [...], "hasMore": true } }
```

## WebSocket Event Format

All gateway events use this structure:

```json
{
  "op": "MESSAGE_CREATE",
  "d": { "id": "...", "channelId": "...", "content": "Hello", "author": { ... } },
  "s": 42
}
```

- `op`: event operation type
- `d`: event data payload
- `s`: sequence number (for resume)
